#: ../../source/escalade_readme.md:3
msgid ""
"A tiny (183B to 210B) and [fast](#benchmarks) utility to ascend parent "
"directories"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/escalade_readme.md:5
msgid ""
"With [escalade](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Escalade), you can scale "
"parent directories until you've found what you're looking for.<br>Given "
"an input file or directory, `escalade` will continue executing your "
"callback function until either:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/escalade_readme.md:7
msgid "the callback returns a truthy value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/escalade_readme.md:8
msgid "`escalade` has reached the system root directory (eg, `/`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/escalade_readme.md:10
msgid ""
"**Important:**<br>Please note that `escalade` only deals with direct "
"ancestry – it will not dive into parents' sibling directories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/escalade_readme.md:14
msgid ""
"**Notice:** As of v3.1.0, `escalade` now includes [Deno "
"support](http://deno.land/x/escalade)! Please see [Deno Usage](#deno) "
"below."
msgstr ""

