#: ../../source/escalade_readme.md:121
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/escalade_readme.md:123
msgid "escalade(input, callback)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/escalade_readme.md:124
msgid "Returns: `string|void` or `Promise<string|void>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/escalade_readme.md:126
msgid ""
"When your `callback` locates a file, `escalade` will resolve/return with "
"an absolute path.<br> If your `callback` was never satisfied, then "
"`escalade` will resolve/return with nothing (undefined)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/escalade_readme.md:129
msgid ""
"**Important:**<br>The `sync` and `async` versions share the same "
"API.<br>The **only** difference is that `sync` is not Promise-based."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/escalade_readme.md:131
msgid "input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/escalade_readme.md:132
msgid "Type: `string`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/escalade_readme.md:134
msgid "The path from which to start ascending."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/escalade_readme.md:136
msgid ""
"This may be a file or a directory path.<br>However, when `input` is a "
"file, `escalade` will begin with its parent directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/escalade_readme.md:138
msgid ""
"**Important:** Unless given an absolute path, `input` will be resolved "
"from `process.cwd()` location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/escalade_readme.md:140
msgid "callback"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/escalade_readme.md:141
msgid "Type: `Function`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/escalade_readme.md:143
msgid ""
"The callback to execute for each ancestry level. It always is given two "
"arguments:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/escalade_readme.md:145
msgid "`dir` - an absolute path of the current parent directory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/escalade_readme.md:146
msgid "`names` - a list (`string[]`) of contents _relative to_ the `dir` parent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/escalade_readme.md:148
msgid "**Note:** The `names` list can contain names of files _and_ directories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/escalade_readme.md:150
msgid ""
"When your callback returns a _falsey_ value, then `escalade` will "
"continue with `dir`'s parent directory, re-invoking your callback with "
"new argument values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/escalade_readme.md:152
msgid ""
"When your callback returns a string, then `escalade` stops iteration "
"immediately.<br> If the string is an absolute path, then it's left as is."
" Otherwise, the string is resolved into an absolute path _from_ the `dir`"
" that housed the satisfying condition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/escalade_readme.md:155
msgid ""
"**Important:** Your `callback` can be a `Promise/AsyncFunction` when "
"using the \"async\" version of `escalade`."
msgstr ""

